.TH PROOFIX 1 "October 2026" "proofix 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
proofix \- fix typos and punctuation in Markdown, under audit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B proofix
.I input.md
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B proofix
.RB [ \-\-setup " | " \-\-check\-endpoint ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B proofix
corrects typos and punctuation in a Markdown file. Every change is one
bounded, logged, reasoned edit; the model never rewrites prose. Run it
after
.BR stylefix (1).
.PP
Five tiers, numbered as in \-\-help and the README:
.TP
.B 0 hygiene
Text that renders fine but is not what it looks like. HTML entities that
Markdown can carry as plain characters (&#32; is a space, &quot; a quote,
&mdash; a dash) are decoded; entities that would change Markdown's parsing
(&lt;, &gt;, &amp;) or carry meaning (&nbsp;) are left alone and reported.
Zero-width spaces, byte-order marks, soft hyphens and control characters
are removed. Windows line endings and decomposed accents are normalised
first. Every change is logged.
.TP
.B 1 mechanical
A space before a comma or period, a missing space after one, doubled
punctuation, doubled words, known misspellings. Found by LanguageTool's
single-answer rules and the typos tool; applied outright.
.TP
.B 2 adjudicated
Unknown words and grammar rules with candidate fixes. LanguageTool
proposes; a language model picks one or KEEP from the sentence and the rule's
message.
.TP
.B 3 compounds and consistency
How a compound is written: closed, hyphenated or open ("cyberattack",
"non-profit", "long term"), and terms the document capitalises two ways.
Candidates come from the dictionaries: an open or hyphenated pair whose
closed form is a word, a non-word that splits into two words, or anything
the document writes two ways. The model chooses closed, hyphenated, open
or KEEP, told which dictionary rules (Merriam-Webster for US, Oxford for
UK) and that a compound modifier before a noun is hyphenated while a noun
phrase is open, so "a third party" survives and "third party assessors"
does not.
.TP
.B 4 commas
Comma placement, which no rule engine detects. The model returns the
sentence with commas corrected; a diff guard admits only insertions and
deletions of commas and rejects anything else. Comma splices and other
faults the model notices are reported as notes, not changed. Serial
commas are left to stylefix's style guide.
.PP
Code, link targets, URLs, HTML and front matter are never touched.
LanguageTool runs twice: mechanical fixes first, then judgement calls on
the cleaned text.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " FILE"
Default: the input name with .proofed before the extension.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-in\-place
Overwrite the input.
.TP
.BR \-\-target " {us|uk}"
Variety the document is written in. Default us.
.TP
.BI \-\-accept " FILE"
Extra words never flagged as misspelled. ~/.config/proofix/accept.txt,
\&./.proofix/accept.txt and stylefix's accept lists are also honoured.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-lt
Skip LanguageTool: its tier 1 fixes (typos still runs) and all of tier 2.
.TP
.BR \-\-lt\-level " {default|picky}"
LanguageTool rule level.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-typos
Skip the typos pre-pass.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-hygiene
Skip the hygiene tier.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-consistency
Skip the compounds and consistency tier.
.TP
.BI \-\-style " GUIDE"
Style guide, used only for its hyphenation habit: ap hyphenates less.
.TP
.BR \-\-commas " {gated|all|none}"
Which sentences the comma tier sends to the model. gated (default): those
with a comma, an introductory opener, a clause trigger, or clauses joined
by a conjunction. all: every sentence. none: skip the tier.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-commas
Same as
.BR "\-\-commas none" .
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-sentences " N"
Cap on sentences sent to the comma tier.
.TP
.BR \-\-optional\-commas " {leave|add}"
Commas that are optional by convention: leave as written (default) or
add.
.TP
.BR \-\-llm " {auto|ollama|none}"
.B auto
(default) uses the endpoint from, highest first, the flags below,
.BR PROOFIX_LLM_* ,
.IR ~/.config/proofix/config.toml ,
.B ADJUDICATE_LLM_*
and
.IR ~/.config/adjudicate/config.toml ,
or else a local Ollama with a model pulled, or else no model.
.B ollama
uses the local Ollama server only, ignoring configured endpoints.
.B none
uses no model: tier 2's fixes are listed for review, not applied, tier 3
is skipped and sentences are not checked for commas; tiers 0 and 1 still
apply.
.TP
.BI \-\-url " URL"
Any OpenAI-compatible base URL ending in /v1. Overrides every configured url.
A \-\-url or PROOFIX_LLM_URL drops keys set in lower layers; set
PROOFIX_LLM_KEY (or \fBapi_key_env\fR in the same config file) alongside it.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " NAME"
Model name at the endpoint. If no layer sets one, the server's first listed model.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SEC"
Seconds per model request, a positive number. Default 120, or
\fBtimeout\fR in config.toml.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-confidence " X"
Decisions below this are not applied. Default 0.8.
.TP
.BI \-\-parallel " N"
Concurrent model requests. Default 4.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache " FILE" ", " \-\-no\-cache
Decision cache, default .proofix/cache.json (commas in commas.json next to it).
.TP
.BI \-\-report " FILE" ", " \-\-no\-report
Markdown report, default <output>.report.md.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print a diff, write nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-changes
Print every change to standard error as it is made.
.TP
.B \-\-setup
Ask where the model is (local Ollama, a hosted OpenAI-compatible API, or a
self-hosted server), test it, and save the answer as the
.B [llm]
table of
.I ~/.config/adjudicate/config.toml
(shared with stylefix) or
.IR ~/.config/proofix/config.toml .
An existing table is shown and replaced only on confirmation, after a
backup to
.IR config.toml.bak .
Needs a terminal. Ends by running the check below.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-endpoint
Print the endpoint proofix would use, one line per setting with the layer
it came from (a key is never shown), then list the server's models and
send one small request. Honours
.BR \-\-llm ", " \-\-url ", " \-\-model " and " \-\-timeout .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Report model batches on standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage summary and exit.
.SH PERFORMANCE
On a 20-page document (8,000 words) with a local 27B model and 8 parallel
requests: LanguageTool 4.5 s per pass; the comma tier 19 s for the 260
sentences that pass the gate; about a minute in all. Linear in length.
Decisions are cached by sentence.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR PROOFIX_LLM_URL ", " PROOFIX_LLM_MODEL ", " PROOFIX_LLM_KEY
Endpoint, model and API key for proofix; below the flags, above the config
files.
.TP
.BR ADJUDICATE_LLM_URL ", " ADJUDICATE_LLM_MODEL ", " ADJUDICATE_LLM_KEY
The same, shared with stylefix; below
.I ~/.config/proofix/config.toml
and above
.IR ~/.config/adjudicate/config.toml .
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
Ollama base URL. Default http://localhost:11434.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/proofix/config.toml
.TQ
.I ~/.config/adjudicate/config.toml
Table
.B [llm]
with keys
.BR url ", " model ", " api_key " or " api_key_env ", " timeout ", " thinking_switch .
The first applies to proofix only; the second is shared with stylefix.
.TP
.IR ~/.config/proofix/accept.txt ", " ~/.config/stylefix/accept.txt ", " .stylefix/accept.txt ", " .proofix/accept.txt
Words never flagged as misspelled, one per line.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Finished. For
.BR \-\-check\-endpoint " and " \-\-setup :
the endpoint answers.
.TP
.B 1
.BR \-\-check\-endpoint " or " \-\-setup :
no endpoint, or it does not answer; or setup was cancelled or declined.
.TP
.B 2
Input file missing, LanguageTool failed, or an invalid endpoint
configuration (the message names the file and key). For
.BR \-\-setup :
standard input is not a terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stylefix (1),
.BR languagetool (1),
.BR typos (1).
.PP
Full documentation: https://github.com/AndrewBroz/proofix
